{%- comment -%}
  Prince Tires — Terms of Use / Terms of Service
  Tailored for: tire retail, online store, in-store + booking-based services,
  wholesale portal, Calgary AB. References Alberta Consumer Protection Act,
  Alberta Sale of Goods Act, and standard limitation-of-liability boilerplate.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign legal_name      = section.settings.legal_name      | default: 'Prince Tires'
  assign business_addr   = section.settings.business_addr   | default: 'Calgary, Alberta, Canada'
  assign contact_email   = section.settings.contact_email   | default: 'info@princetires.ca'
  assign contact_phone   = section.settings.contact_phone   | default: '403 452 4283'
  assign effective_date  = section.settings.effective_date  | default: 'May 5, 2026'
-%}

<article class="pt-policy">
  <header class="pt-policy__head">
    <p class="pt-policy__eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="pt-policy__title">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="pt-policy__meta">Effective: {{ effective_date }} &middot; Last updated: {{ effective_date }}</p>
  </header>

  <nav class="pt-policy__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <p class="pt-policy__toc-title">Contents</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#terms-1">1. Acceptance of these Terms</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-2">2. Who may use the site &amp; services</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-3">3. Customer accounts</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-4">4. Orders, pricing &amp; availability</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-5">5. Payment, taxes &amp; currency</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-6">6. Shipping &amp; delivery</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-7">7. Service appointments &amp; bookings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-8">8. Installation &amp; workmanship</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-9">9. Tire warranty &amp; manufacturer claims</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-10">10. Vehicle drop-off, storage &amp; release</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-11">11. Wholesale &amp; trade accounts</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-12">12. Intellectual property</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-13">13. User content &amp; reviews</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-14">14. Acceptable use</a></li>
      <li><a href="#terms-15">15. Disclaimers, liability &amp; governing law</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="terms-1" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>1. Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
    <p>These Terms of Use ("Terms") form a legally binding agreement between you and {{ legal_name }} ("we," "us," "our") covering your use of our website at princetires.ca (the "Site"), our online store, our service-booking system, our wholesale portal, our mobile and desktop forms, and any related products or services we provide (collectively, the "Services").</p>
    <p>By using the Site or Services, by creating an account, by placing an order, by booking an appointment, or by accepting these Terms in any other way, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and by our <a href="/pages/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the Site or Services.</p>
    <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Effective" date at the top indicates the current version. Continued use of the Site or Services after a change means you accept the updated Terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-2" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>2. Who may use the site &amp; services</h2>
    <p>You may use the Site and place orders if you are at least 18 years old, have the legal capacity to enter into a contract, and are using the Services for personal or business purposes that comply with these Terms and applicable law. We do not knowingly do business with anyone under 18.</p>
    <p>We may refuse, suspend, or terminate access to the Site or Services to any person at any time, in our reasonable discretion, including where we suspect fraud, abuse, breach of these Terms, or any unlawful conduct.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-3" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>3. Customer accounts</h2>
    <p>You may browse most of the Site without an account, but some features (such as saving vehicles, wholesale pricing, and order history) require one. When creating an account you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accurate, current, and complete information</li>
      <li>Keep your password confidential</li>
      <li>Take responsibility for all activity that occurs under your account</li>
      <li>Notify us promptly at <a href="mailto:{{ contact_email }}">{{ contact_email }}</a> if you suspect unauthorized use</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We are not liable for any loss caused by unauthorized use of your account that you could have prevented by following the practices above.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-4" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>4. Orders, pricing &amp; availability</h2>
    <p>All prices on the Site are shown in Canadian dollars (CAD) and exclude applicable taxes and shipping unless we say otherwise. We try to keep pricing and inventory up to date, but errors and stock changes do happen.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Order acceptance.</strong> Your order is an offer to buy at the displayed price. We accept your offer when we send a confirmation that your order has shipped or been picked up. Until then, we may decline or cancel any order at our sole discretion.</li>
      <li><strong>Pricing errors.</strong> If a product is listed at an obviously incorrect price (for example, due to a typographical or technical error), we may cancel the order and issue a full refund, even after a payment confirmation has been sent.</li>
      <li><strong>Inventory.</strong> Listed items are subject to availability. If a product becomes unavailable after you have paid, we will notify you and offer a comparable substitute or a full refund.</li>
      <li><strong>Quantity limits.</strong> We reserve the right to limit the quantity of any product purchased per customer or per order, and to refuse orders we reasonably believe are placed by resellers without authorization.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-5" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>5. Payment, taxes &amp; currency</h2>
    <p>We accept the payment methods displayed at checkout, which may include Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Interac Online, Apple Pay, Google Pay, and (for approved trade accounts) net-terms invoicing. By submitting payment, you represent that you are authorized to use the payment method.</p>
    <p>We do not store full credit-card numbers. Card data is processed by our PCI-compliant payment processors. Failed or declined transactions may delay or cancel your order.</p>
    <p>All applicable Canadian federal and provincial taxes (including 5% GST) are calculated at checkout based on your billing or shipping address. For purchases shipped or fulfilled outside Alberta, the applicable provincial taxes apply.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-6" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>6. Shipping &amp; delivery</h2>
    <p>Shipping options, lead times, and rates are displayed at checkout and depend on the items, your address, and the courier. We typically ship within 1–3 business days of order confirmation; transit time varies by destination.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Title and risk.</strong> Title and risk of loss to ordered products pass to you when the products are delivered to the courier (FOB origin), unless we agree otherwise in writing.</li>
      <li><strong>Failed deliveries.</strong> If the courier is unable to deliver because of an incorrect address, refusal of delivery, or inability to reach you, we may charge a return-shipping or restocking fee.</li>
      <li><strong>Customs &amp; duties.</strong> For shipments outside Canada, you are responsible for any import duties or taxes.</li>
      <li><strong>Local pickup.</strong> Where local pickup is offered, you must pick up your order within 30 days of the pickup-ready notification. After 30 days unclaimed orders may be re-stocked and refunded less a 15% restocking fee.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-7" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>7. Service appointments &amp; bookings</h2>
    <p>You may book tire installation, balancing, rotation, flat repair, TPMS service, and seasonal swap appointments through our online booking system or by phone or text.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lead time.</strong> Online bookings require a minimum lead time (typically 6 hours). Earlier service may be available by calling us; subject to availability.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirmation.</strong> Your booking is confirmed only when you receive an email or SMS confirmation from us.</li>
      <li><strong>Reschedules &amp; cancellations.</strong> You may reschedule or cancel free of charge using the link in your confirmation email up to 4 hours before your appointment. Within 4 hours of the appointment, no-shows or last-minute cancellations may be subject to a $50 inconvenience fee.</li>
      <li><strong>Late arrivals.</strong> If you arrive more than 15 minutes late, we may need to reschedule your appointment to keep on time for other customers.</li>
      <li><strong>Estimated times.</strong> Quoted service times are estimates; complications discovered during work may extend them. We will tell you if a job will run materially longer than estimated.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-8" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>8. Installation &amp; workmanship</h2>
    <p>We warrant our workmanship on tires we install for 90 days from the date of service against defects in mounting, balancing, and torque. If a workmanship issue arises within 90 days, we will re-perform the service at no charge.</p>
    <p>Our workmanship warranty does <strong>not</strong> cover:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Damage caused by impacts (potholes, curbs, debris) after the install</li>
      <li>Damage caused by neglect, modification, racing, or off-road use</li>
      <li>Pre-existing wheel, rim, suspension, or alignment issues we identified and disclosed at intake</li>
      <li>Tires installed on wheels we did not supply if the wheel turns out to be defective or not appropriate for the tire</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For all installs you give us informed consent to mount, balance, and torque the tires you have purchased, and to perform any related safety inspection, and you confirm that the wheels and vehicle are appropriate for the tires you have selected.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-9" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>9. Tire warranty &amp; manufacturer claims</h2>
    <p>New tires are covered by the manufacturer's tread-life and limited warranty, which we will pass through to you. Manufacturer warranty terms vary by brand and model and are documented on the manufacturer's website or warranty card.</p>
    <p>If a manufacturer-warranty issue arises, we will:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Inspect the tire and document the wear or defect</li>
      <li>Submit a claim to the manufacturer on your behalf where allowed</li>
      <li>Apply any manufacturer credit toward a replacement, with you paying the prorated balance, mounting, balancing, valve stems, taxes, and disposal where the manufacturer does not cover them</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Manufacturer warranties do not generally cover road-hazard damage, improper inflation, neglect, racing, or off-road use. A separate <strong>road-hazard protection plan</strong> may be available at the time of purchase. Coverage details and limits will be provided in writing when you purchase the plan.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-10" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>10. Vehicle drop-off, storage &amp; release</h2>
    <p>When you leave a vehicle with us for service:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You authorize our technicians to test-drive the vehicle a short distance for diagnostic and balance verification.</li>
      <li>You confirm that you are the legal owner of the vehicle (or are duly authorized to authorize service on it).</li>
      <li>You agree that we are not responsible for items left in the vehicle, including aftermarket electronics, valuables, and personal effects.</li>
      <li>You agree to pick up your vehicle within 5 business days of the service-complete notification. After 5 business days a daily storage fee of up to $25 per day may apply.</li>
      <li>If a vehicle is left more than 90 days after the service-complete notification despite our reasonable efforts to contact you, we may treat it as abandoned and dispose of it under the <em>Garage Keepers' Lien Act</em> (Alberta) and recoup unpaid charges from the proceeds.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Old tires removed from your vehicle are disposed of under our environmental tire-disposal contract. You consent to that disposal unless you tell us at intake that you wish to keep the old tires.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-11" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>11. Wholesale &amp; trade accounts</h2>
    <p>Wholesale pricing is available only to approved trade accounts (auto repair shops, dealerships, fleet operators, and similar businesses). Trade accounts are subject to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Approval based on a completed application, business documentation, and (where applicable) a credit check</li>
      <li>Resale-only restrictions (wholesale stock may not be re-listed on consumer marketplaces without our written approval)</li>
      <li>Net payment terms agreed in writing; overdue balances may be charged interest at 2% per month (24% per year) and may result in account suspension</li>
      <li>Minimum order quantities, freight terms, and return policies as set out in your trade-account agreement</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Wholesale orders are governed by these Terms together with any signed trade-account agreement; in the case of conflict, the trade-account agreement controls.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-12" class="pt-policy__section">
