    <p>All content on the Site — including text, graphics, logos, photographs, illustrations, software, layouts, the "{{ legal_name }}" word mark, and any trade marks displayed — is owned by or licensed to us and is protected by Canadian and international intellectual-property law.</p>
    <p>We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to access and use the Site for personal, non-commercial purposes (or, for trade-account holders, internal business purposes). You may not copy, reproduce, republish, scrape, frame, mirror, sell, sublicense, or create derivative works from any part of the Site without our prior written consent, except as expressly permitted by these Terms or by law.</p>
    <p>Tire and parts manufacturer trade marks shown on the Site are the property of their respective owners and are used to describe the products we sell.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-13" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>13. User content &amp; reviews</h2>
    <p>If you submit reviews, photos, comments, suggestions, or other content to us or to our public profiles ("User Content"), you grant us a worldwide, royalty-free, perpetual, non-exclusive licence to use, reproduce, modify, publish, and display that content in connection with our business and to promote our products and services.</p>
    <p>You confirm that any User Content you submit:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is your original work or you have the right to share it</li>
      <li>Is honest and accurate</li>
      <li>Does not infringe anyone's intellectual-property, privacy, or other rights</li>
      <li>Is not threatening, harassing, defamatory, obscene, or unlawful</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may remove or refuse to publish User Content at any time without notice or explanation.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-14" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>14. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>When using the Site or Services, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the Site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of these Terms</li>
      <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Site, servers, or networks (for example, by sending excessive requests, scraping at scale, or attempting to bypass authentication)</li>
      <li>Use bots, scrapers, or automated tools to copy or extract content without our written consent</li>
      <li>Reverse-engineer or attempt to derive source code from any part of our Services</li>
      <li>Impersonate another person or misrepresent your affiliation with anyone</li>
      <li>Submit fraudulent orders, payments, or wholesale applications</li>
      <li>Send unsolicited commercial messages through any of our forms or contact channels</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Violations may result in account suspension or termination, cancelled orders, blocked access to the Site, and (where applicable) civil or criminal liability.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="terms-15" class="pt-policy__section">
    <h2>15. Disclaimers, liability &amp; governing law</h2>
    <h3>15.1 Disclaimers</h3>
    <p>The Site and Services are provided <strong>"as is"</strong> and <strong>"as available."</strong> Except for express warranties stated in writing — and except for the implied conditions of fitness for purpose, acceptable quality, and matching description that apply under the Alberta <em>Sale of Goods Act</em> and the <em>Consumer Protection Act</em> for consumer transactions and that <strong>cannot lawfully be excluded</strong> — we disclaim, to the fullest extent permitted by law, all warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of viruses.</p>

    <h3>15.2 Limitation of liability</h3>
    <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total aggregate liability to you for any claim arising out of or relating to the Site, the Services, or any product purchased from us is limited to the greater of (a) the amount you paid us for the specific product or service giving rise to the claim, or (b) one hundred Canadian dollars ($100 CAD).</p>
    <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, lost profits, lost data, lost goodwill, or business interruption, even if we have been advised of the possibility of those damages.</p>
    <p>Nothing in these Terms limits our liability for fraud, fraudulent misrepresentation, death or personal injury caused by our negligence, or any other liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited under Alberta law.</p>

    <h3>15.3 Indemnity</h3>
    <p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {{ legal_name }} and its directors, employees, and contractors from and against any claims, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your breach of these Terms, your violation of any law, or your infringement of any third-party right.</p>

    <h3>15.4 Governing law &amp; jurisdiction</h3>
    <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Alberta and the federal laws of Canada that apply in Alberta, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. The courts of Alberta have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Services, except that we may seek injunctive or equitable relief in any competent court.</p>

    <h3>15.5 Severability &amp; entire agreement</h3>
    <p>If any provision of these Terms is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect. These Terms (together with our Privacy Policy and any applicable trade-account agreement) form the entire agreement between you and us regarding the Site and Services and supersede any prior or contemporaneous understandings.</p>

    <h3>15.6 How to contact us</h3>
    <p class="pt-policy__contact">
      <strong>{{ legal_name }}</strong><br>
      {{ business_addr }}<br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:{{ contact_email }}">{{ contact_email }}</a><br>
      Phone: <a href="tel:{{ contact_phone | replace: ' ', '' }}">{{ contact_phone }}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</article>

